- op: discuss  # 10d5
  at: '2026-09-18T00:38:06Z'  # 10d5
  by: agent  # 10d5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 10d5
  clock: 4  # 10d5
  nonce: 10d5  # 10d5
  message: "TWO OF THREE VERDICTS SHIPPED (PR #1034). THE THIRD IS YOURS, so this row\nmoves to needs_human_review rather than done -- the condition in its TITLE\nstill holds, and closing it would assert a fix that did not happen.\n\nSHIPPED:\n\n(1) THE HOST RULE IS NOW WRITTEN DOWN, at the fields rather than inferred.\npass_silence.py carries the measured three-route table -- pre-filter (75,\n-> skipped_passes), bare AnalysisResult() return (7, -> skipped_passes), run\nwith files_analyzed=0 (26, -> analysis_runs) -- and states plainly that the\nhost encodes producer registration and implementation detail, not a property\nof the silence. It also records that the value split is NOT symmetric with the\nhost split: three values live only on each host, and the overlap is exactly\nno_candidate_files and unreported, which is where 80% of the volume sits.\n\n(2) census_silence() UNIONS THE TWO, preserving each host's own absence rule\nbecause they differ for a reason. Built over the PASS CATALOGUE, not over\nruns + skips -- that union is structurally blind to the third outcome, which\nis real: rust_analyzer put 669 nodes and 637 edges into artifacts while\nappearing in neither list (WI-didag). unaccounted is None when no catalogue\nwas supplied and () when one was and nothing was missing; an empty tuple would\nclaim \"I checked\" where None says \"I could not\".\n\n    AND THE READER IS WIRED. emit_unaccounted_warning runs on every survey\n    beside the two existing summaries, with an AST test asserting cli.py CALLS\n    it. This is the signal that would have surfaced WI-didag on the run that\n    introduced it instead of a month later.\n\nSELF-REPORT: the first draft of census_silence built `unaccounted` from the\npasses that had a REASON, so a pass that EMITTED -- which has an analysis_runs\nrow and correctly no reason -- was reported as missing from the catalogue.\nThat is the same absent-versus-empty conflation this row is about, committed\ninside the helper written to expose it. The test caught it before it shipped;\npresence is now tracked separately and pinned by its own regression test.\n\nNOT SHIPPED, AND NOT AN AGENT'S CALL: verdict (3), changing the ROUTING so the\nhost becomes a function of the fact. The 130-of-162 split still exists exactly\nas this row's title says; what changed is that it is now documented and a\nconsumer can get a right answer without knowing about the WI-jadig pre-filter.\nChanging the routing touches the WI-didil AR-or-skip completeness contract and\nis adjacent to the decision ADR-0056 item 5 already reserves to you.\n\nTHE THREE OPTIONS, unchanged from the audit, with (2) now done:\n  (1) document only                -- shipped\n  (2) document + union helper      -- shipped\n  (3) make the host a function of the fact -- YOURS\n\nIf you take (3), note it now has THREE outcomes to account for, not two.\n\nRELATED, deliberately left alone: docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1317 still carries\nthe wrong routing sentence (26 of 35 out-of-taxonomy analyzers land in\nanalysis_runs, not skipped_passes as it claims). That is WI-gisor, which was\nnot in this batch, and I did not straddle it."  # 10d5
