- op: discuss  # 542c
  at: '2026-09-18T04:15:23Z'  # 542c
  by: agent  # 542c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 542c
  clock: 6  # 542c
  nonce: 542c  # 542c
  message: "OWNER RULING RECEIVED 2026-09-17, VERDICT A. Shipped in PR #1037 (merged,\norigin/dev = 93fabf5c2d). All three options this row raised are now\ndispositioned, so it closes -- but read the NOT CLAIMED section, because half\nthe title still describes reality and does so BY DECISION.\n\nTHE RULING. Presented as three shapes with their measured costs:\n  A  one name, two hosts        -- CHOSEN\n  B  route by value             -- declined; needs an AnalysisRun for the 75\n                                   pre-filtered passes, which IS ADR-0056\n                                   item 5, reserved to the owner and judged\n                                   wrong there (ABSENT != EMPTY one level up)\n  C  one list, all passes       -- declined; would make half the fields\n                                   structurally inapplicable for half the\n                                   rows, the shape ADR-0040's declared-=>-\n                                   populated discipline and the spec's\n                                   derived_skipped ruling both reject\n\nSHIPPED. `limits.skipped_passes[].skip_reason_code` -> `silence_reason`, the\nname AnalysisRun already used for the same question on the same closed axis.\nSCHEMA_VERSION 0.20.9 -> 0.20.10, breaking for readers of the old key (which\nshipped one version earlier, in the same unreleased window). Nine sites; the\nproducer-side `AnalysisResult.skip_reason_code` kwarg is deliberately NOT\nrenamed, because \"skip\" is apt on a skipped result and\ntest_skip_reason_code_declaration.py gates that kwarg rather than the output.\n\nCLOSURE EVIDENCE, on canonical dev after the merge:\n\n    hypergumbo survey component-model-demo\n      old key present anywhere: False\n      analysis_runs 36 + skipped_passes 83 = 119\n      no_candidate_files: 26 on analysis_runs + 82 on skipped_passes\n\nPinned by test_pass_silence.py::TestOneFactOneName -- one test on the\nproduction dispatcher asserting every skip entry carries `silence_reason` and\nnone carries the old key, one asserting both hosts serialize the same key so\ncensus_silence can union without a per-host alias.\n\nNOT CLAIMED, AND THIS IS THE HALF THAT MATTERS. The second clause of this\nrow's title -- \"the host is chosen by taxonomy membership + analyzer return\nstyle, not by any property of the silence\" -- IS STILL TRUE. Verdict A does\nnot touch routing and was not intended to. 130 of 162 passes still carry\nno_candidate_files split 48/82 across two hosts; what changed is that a\nconsumer no longer needs to know WHICH host will answer in order to ask the\nquestion. Anyone reading this closed row as \"the split is fixed\" is reading it\nwrong.\n\nWHERE THE RESIDUAL LIVES, so it is not orphaned by this closure: ADR-0056\n§\"What would change this decision\" item 5 is the standing home for the routing\nquestion and remains reserved to the owner. A correction note was added to\nthat ADR in the same PR recording that the field was renamed, that the\nre-hosting verdict stands, and that the routing was deliberately left alone.\nThis row is closed because its three options are dispositioned, NOT because\nthe host boundary became principled.\n\nALSO IN THE SAME PR, deliberately: WI-gisor's spec sentence, because it is the\nsame paragraph and fixing them separately meant writing section 1317 twice."  # 542c
